# Longer waits advance peroxide kinetics
# Give identical peroxide samples four different waits. What does the registered kinetic network do as modeled time advances?
# Intermediate mission. Inspect the complete inventory after 30, 60, 120 and
# 240 seconds: peroxide decomposition advances while hydrogen and oxygen remain
# accounted for.
#
# Model boundary: this is a test of the bench's registered peroxide network,
# not a new empirical rate law. Real decomposition also depends on concentration,
# temperature, light, impurities, surfaces and catalysts. Use only
# teacher-prepared dilute peroxide, eye protection
# and clean compatible apparatus for any physical comparison. Do not ingest it
# or return used material to its stock container.
register lv2
add v1 water 200mL
add v1 H2O2 0.01mol
wait 30s
inspect v1
new
add v2 water 200mL
add v2 H2O2 0.01mol
wait 60s
inspect v2
new
add v3 water 200mL
add v3 H2O2 0.01mol
wait 120s
inspect v3
new
add v4 water 200mL
add v4 H2O2 0.01mol
wait 240s
inspect v4
